{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - User - Session - Okta Session Used From More Than One Country or Network [table]",
	"Description": "Finds Okta sessions that were used from more than one country or more than one network operator. A stolen session cookie replayed from the adversary's own infrastructure shows up here, because the same externalSessionId turns up resolving to two different places.\n\nCountries and operators come from Okta's own client.geographicalContext and securityContext, falling back to the maxmind and asn_db resources from the Gravwell Network Enrichment kit for events that arrive without them.\n\nNote on device token hashes: Okta legitimately issues several dtHash values inside one session as authentication progresses, so dtHash count alone is not a usable signal and is reported here as context rather than used as the threshold.\n\nThresholds: 2 or more distinct countries, or 2 or more distinct network operators, per session. Edit the eval near the end of the query to tune them.\n\nThis detection uses stats, so it renders as a table rather than shipping raw entries.\n\nReference(s):\n- https://developer.okta.com/docs/reference/api/event-types/\n- https://developer.okta.com/docs/api/openapi/okta-management/management/tag/SystemLog/\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
	"ScheduledType": "search",
	"GUID": "5af0530b-c26f-55ea-baac-c87fb12863de",
	"SearchReference": "9e2cd5fc-5c1f-5e06-9f1e-25b6f06cc8a4"
}